# Licensed Avid AMA/ACF/AAF payload stays local. Only these first-party layout
# README files are public; directories are traversable so the placeholders work.
/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/**
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/**/
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/README.md
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/amasdk/include/README.md
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/amasdk/lib/debug/README.md
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/amasdk/lib/release/README.md
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/acfsdk/inc/README.md
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/acfsdk/utils/README.md
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/acfsdk/schema/README.md
!/ThirdParty/AvidSDK/aafsdk/include/README.md
/ThirdParty/AvidSDK.manifest.sha256
**/AMA-SDK*/
**/LocalEvidence/

# Local research and host debugging records are not release documentation.
/docs/AMA-output-debug-2026-09-30.md
/Tests/ProResEncoderAMA/ColorFrameProbe.swift
/docs/MediaComposer_AVX_ProRes_Plan_2026-09-22/

